referenceFunction.generalComment:
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg ETBE, at the oil refinery. ETBE can be incorporated at up to 15% vol. in gasoline, as an oxygenate, according to the current (2005) European Norms. Anhydrous bioethanol is produced from rye, in the RER context. Naphtha is used as a proxy dataset for isobutene. This process is applied in France and Spain and possibly in Germany. Fossil and biogenic carbon contents are respectively 45.4% and 25.4%, according to the respective shares of isobutene (53% wt.) and ethanol (47% wt.).;
CAS number: 000637-92-3; 
Formula: C6H14O; 
Synonyms: 2-ethoxy-2-methylpropane, 2-methyl-2-ethoxypropane, ETBE, ethyl tert-butyl ether, ethyl tertiary butyl ether, ethyl tertio butyl ether, ethyl tert-butyl oxide, tert-butyl ethyl ether; 
UUID: 1196dd71-ef0f-31d8-9085-e58accfd9605
